repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/digital-to-wave-2-thz-validity"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC engineering-validity study of the THz human-wave interface (HWI)
  equations in Mun Seok Lee's preprint "Digital to Wave: LGD In Situ Wave
  Memory-Human Wave Integrated Interface-Metaverse Hologram- Wave Affective
  AI" (Part II). It inventories the quantitative content of Part II by page
  and classifies each item as simulatable, dimensionally or physically
  checkable, or too vague to implement; checks the HWI equations
  dimensionally; evaluates them with cited standard reference values (THz
  absorption and refractive index of water, membrane parameters, an extreme
  second-order susceptibility upper bound, ICNIRP exposure limits, air
  breakdown, heating and thermal times); and runs a seeded, protocol-locked
  synthetic channel benchmark that carries the Part I signed-amplitude sine
  encoding (vendored verbatim from the Digital to Wave Testbench v0.4.1)
  through square-law rectification, a 100 Hz membrane low-pass,
  Beer-Lambert depth loss and two-tone THz beating, with nominal, calibrated
  and oracle receivers, Wilson intervals, closed-form predictions and exact
  McNemar tests. No physical, biological or safety claim is made. The
  preprints' author has not reviewed or endorsed this software.
keywords:
  - synthetic-data
  - engineering validity
  - dimensional analysis
  - terahertz
  - Beer-Lambert
  - optical rectification
  - signal processing
  - matched filter
  - reproducibility
  - wilson-interval
  - scientific-software
  - Digital to Wave
